      "writtenOn": "2026-06-29T07:29:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`File` overrides `write_hash` but not `equals`. The default `StarlarkValue::equals` returns `Ok(false)` (\"Type is only equal via a pointer\"), so two `File` values for the same interned path hash equal but compare *un*equal in Starlark: `declare_file(\"x\") \u003d\u003d declare_file(\"x\")` is `False`, and a Starlark dict/set keyed by `File` never dedups them. That contradicts the pointer-equality intent documented above this type.\n\nEvery hashable builtin in starlark-rust (`bytes`, `bigint`) overrides both `write_hash` and `equals` - should we do the same here and in `label.rs`?\n\n```rust\nfn equals(\u0026self, other: Value\u003c\u0027v\u003e) -\u003e starlark::Result\u003cbool\u003e {\n    Ok(other.downcast_ref::\u003cFile\u003e().is_some_and(|o| self \u003d\u003d o))\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "b83bfa521fe75cf5b21e3e1aba86580b1bda6c9e",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
